    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Polynesian kingdom created by the Pōmare family, who used European guns and allies to rise above Tahiti’s rival chiefs from about 1788.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a>’s victory at Fei Pi in 1815 made Tahiti a Christian kingdom, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>’s first written law code in 1819.</li><li>Anglo-French rivalry led to a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1842, a war in 1844–1847 and annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1880.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The landing of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> missionaries at Matavai Bay on 5 March 1797 is still a public holiday in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, the Arrivée de l’Évangile.</p></aside>
    </section>

